<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">
    <!--
        Type tokens, the counterpart to the colour tokens in Brushes.xaml.

        Before this file, "Segoe UI" was written out in 26 places across 16
        files and the sizes were loose literals, so there was no single place
        to change the UI font.

        Sizes are named for their role, not their value, so a caller says what
        it means and the scale can be retuned in one edit:

            Small   11   secondary labels, section headers
            Normal  12   the default for controls
            Large   13   text inputs, anything that has to be comfortable to read

        These are plain resources, so they are only usable from a Style setter
        or an element attribute, never from inside a ControlTemplate body. That
        is the VSTO rule (see the note in OfficePalette.xaml), and it is why the
        control dictionaries in this folder still inline their font values.

        Note this is the UI chrome font, and has nothing to do with the Hebrew
        document fonts that WpfLib.Helpers.FontsProvider enumerates.
    -->

    <FontFamily x:Key="UiFontFamily">Segoe UI</FontFamily>

    <sys:Double x:Key="FontSizeSmall">11</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="FontSizeNormal">12</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="FontSizeLarge">13</sys:Double>

</ResourceDictionary>
